        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:36",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:seven-choices:2",
            "text": "Since a new year has started, time lies before us like a blank page, waiting to be filled with writing. We are all busy people, and we sometimes feel that life is working against our writing ambitions and pushing them aside. Yet the most productive writers are the busiest. Then how can we make sure we get our writing done in 2025?"
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:37",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:seven-choices:3",
            "text": "Overcoming self-doubt and fear is the key to unlocking your potential. We all have a voice in our head that keeps telling us we can’t succeed. Most of the time, the real reason why we avoid writing is that we’re afraid of failing. It’s simpler to complain about being too busy than to face our fears. To solve this problem, we can try to understand what we’re scared of, deal with it, and then focus on moving forward."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:38",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:seven-choices:4",
            "text": "A simple way to find more time to write is to give yourself a clear goal. It needs to be SMART: specific, measurable, achievable, realistic and time-bound. For example, writing 1,500 words in a week might be realistic. If you successfully meet your target, you could give yourself a small reward: buy a new notebook or pen, go for a long walk, or take a day off from writing and just do something completely different."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:39",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:seven-choices:5",
            "text": "Do something different if your current approach isn’t working. As Henry Ford once said, “If you do what you’ve always done, you’ll get what you’ve always got”! This could mean writing with a notebook and pen rather than the computer you also use for work. Try varying your approach and see if it helps."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:40",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:seven-choices:6",
            "text": "Above all, you should prioritize writing over other things. Most successful writers have caring responsibilities, occupations outside the home, and the necessary everyday tasks they all need to complete. Yet they still manage to write. What they have in common is that they treat writing as important. So, if you want to make 2025 the year when you get your writing project done, look at how you use your time with a fresh eye."
          }
        ],
